            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Later Composers</strong><br>\nHaydn's work had a profound impact on later composers, most notably Ludwig van Beethoven, who was once his student. Haydn's influence can be seen in the structures, melodies, and harmonic progressions that became standard in classical music. His role as a mentor to Beethoven also highlights his contribution to the transition from the Classical to the Romantic era in music history.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Life and Character</strong><br>\nKnown for his sense of humor, which often reflected in his music, Haydn was well-regarded by his contemporaries. Despite the long periods he spent away from his wife during his service at the Esterházy court, their marriage was troubled and childless. Haydn formed a close relationship with the Esterházy family, particularly with Prince Nikolaus, who appreciated his musical abilities and provided him with the resources to compose and perform.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nHaydn died in 1809 at the age of 77, after a career that saw the establishment of the classical style in music. His death marked the end of an era, but his influence persisted. His contributions to musical form and harmony shaped the direction of Western classical music, and his works remain central to the repertoire. Haydn is remembered as the \"Father of the Symphony\" and the \"Father of the String Quartet,\" honoring his pivotal role in the history of music.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3d655444-fd55-42f7-aba2-16a16db7dc58"
